A1. These are not so hot. ~ WINTERS
A7. Any bright thing can do this. ~ REFLECT
A13. This is often sitting or running while standing. ~ ARMY
A14. To flow out. ~ EBB
A16. Too many sweets reached for will do this. ~ CLOY
A17. This is seen at various stages. ~ REVUE
A19. Dora thinks this is oatmeal. ~ CRUEL
A20. Ships in the night pass here. ~ ABEAM
A22. Spain's national pastime. ~ SIESTA
A24. Between more and more. ~ AND
A25. Mexican whoopee. ~ FIESTA
A26. The initials of his name. ~ HN
A27. This is a daily visitor to Coney Island. ~ TIDE
A29. Man must be skinned to get these. ~ FURS
A30. A high road. ~ EL
A32. Summer residents and some are not. ~ COTTAGERS
A36. A type seldom seen in a ballroom. ~ PICA
A39. The sponsor of a steamer. ~ STANLEY
A40. This is often used with feathers. ~ FUSS
A42. No trimmings on this. ~ NUDE
A44. These are always in a con game. ~ ANTIS
A45. This always comes before der Kaiser. ~ HOCH
A46. A Saturday night fadeout. ~ SALARY
A47. The last thing you will ever kick. ~ BUCKET
A48. Nice little unlawful things. ~ NIPS
A49. If you try to look thru a Woolworth diamond you won't get stoneblind but you'll get this in the eye. ~ PASTE
A52. What an electric plant grows from. ~ BULB
A53. The longer you work the less of this you get. ~ REST
A54. This may be petty but sometimes it's grand. ~ LARCENY
A56. A sad place for a parting. ~ SEAM
A58. Wool coverings. ~ BANDANNAS
A60. Exclamation meaning almost anything. ~ AH
A62. I give up. ~ CEDE
A63. A narrow coin collector. ~ SLOT
A65. Old town whoopee (abbr.). ~ HT
A66. To set up the results of an upset. ~ RETIDY
A68. This is about the centre of the population of Japan. ~ OBI
A70. This is a loving one. ~ EROTIC
A72. Something a well-groomed person faces daily. ~ IMAGE
A73. He works for nothing at all. ~ SLAVE
A74. The common sense of all gold diggers. ~ TOUCH
A75. You can get this out of step. ~ PACE
A77. The best kind of humor and the worst kind of law. ~ DRY
A78. We all love this person. ~ SELF
A79. This is a pretty pickle. ~ GHERKIN
A80. Bested. ~ WORSTED

D1. A kind of ship which is generally bow down. ~ WORSHIP
D2. What the maid of honor goes thru for the bride. ~ NAVE
D3. The biggest bust Teddy made. ~ TRUST
D4. Something you put up with. ~ EMETIC
D5. Something you trip over (abbr.). ~ RY
D6. This means a lot to you. ~ ABUNDANT
D8. Initial letters of every country. ~ EC
D9. Knacks. ~ FLAIRS
D10. These are found near drums. ~ LOBES
D11. Two of these look better than one. ~ EYES
D12. This is two or more hot ones. ~ TAMALES
D14. Time used in making crossword puzzles. ~ ERA
D15. One place where lying does you some good. ~ BED
D18. This is a German one. ~ EIN
D21. Replenished the inner man. ~ ATE
D23. More than one fuss. ~ ADOS
D25. This will make you mad. ~ FURY
D28. Girl's name. ~ ETTA
D29. What the lawyer pleads for. ~ FEES
D31. He will give you a treat for sore eyes. ~ OCULIST
D33. An outlawed vessel. ~ TANKARD
D34. What brightness can do. ~ GLISTEN
D35. Bright bits by the tongues of vamps. ~ BUCKLES
D37. This is silly. ~ INANE
D38. To fit. ~ ADAPT
D40. Here's the point. ~ FOCUS
D41. The cake eater's girl friend. ~ SHEBA
D43. He who hesitates says this (pl.). ~ ERS
D45. This goes around in the midst of tired things. ~ HUB
D49. An invention that will enable you to see thru a ten-foot wall. ~ PANE
D50. This makes it hard to see the point. ~ SCABBARD
D51. Nasal letters. ~ ENNS
D53. Crying out loud. ~ ROARING
D54. Something used with birds, bugs and fingers. ~ LADY
D55. You get the blues after going there for a while. ~ YALE
D57. Mated. ~ MATCHED
D58. The deck that decorates. ~ BEDECK
D59. He divides sheep from goats. ~ SORTER
D61. Not so long ago this was the thin edge of very little but now it's gone down in the world. ~ HEM
D62. This comes from the mouth of many an orator. ~ CIGAR
D64. Plumber's alibis. ~ TOOLS
D65. A drunk's vocabulary. ~ HIC
D67. This is bad to handle when it's red. ~ TAPE
D68. One thing a gold digger doesn't try to get. ~ OLD
D69. This sticks mighty close to the old home. ~ IVY
D71. The end of the rooster. ~ TUFT
D76. That is, reversed. ~ EI
D78. The meaning here is like this. ~ SO


